ple  themselves because they seem  so real and unchangeable but these  characters and the story surrounding  them have undergone  many drafts and revisions the term sith  was actually first  used in an early draft of a new hope  this was back when the entire saga  still lived in george lucas's head as  the star wars  while most of the changes and omissions  in the final theatrical release of a new  hope were for the better  it's pretty cool that the sith made  their appearance decades later with  darth maul hunting down  our heroes an intimidating warrior like  darth maul  seems like an obvious candidate to be  the apprentice for the sith lord darth  sidious  but he wasn't necessarily the first  choice  here's where darth maul's family comes  into play like most powerful men darth  maul had an even more powerful mother  who raised him  mother talzin was the leader of the  night sisters a group of force sensitive  dathomirian women  who used the power of the force for  their own purposes  but since the force imbues its users  with otherworldly abilities  the night sisters were branded as  witches on their home planet  darth sidious knew of this powerful clan  of force users  and came to dathomir seeking an  apprentice he intended to pass on the  ways of the sith to a student who would  help him further his goals of destroying  the galactic republic  and the jedi order originally sidious  told mother talzin that he wanted her to  be his apprentice  a powerful force user in her own right  she seemed like a natural choice  but sidious betrayed her in a twisted  mockery of the jedi practice of teaching  younglings  sidious abducted her son the young darth  maul and raised him in the ways of the  sith  as with so much of the massive sprawling  lore of star wars there was still more  to uncover  in the star wars universe the term sith  originates from an ancient race of force  sensitive humanoids  hailing originally from the planet  moriband these people were known as the  sith and the entire race had a penchant  for the dark side  this force-wielding species eventually  dispersed and spread throughout the  galaxy  in the name of their once mighty  civilization came to refer to the order  of force users who allied with the dark  side  the sith had dark red skin and bodies  with bone spurs not too dissimilar to  darth maul  but while maul was one of the first  beings to be associated with the word  sith  he isn't actually a member of the sith  species  he hails from the planet dathomir  another world known for its force using  inhabitants darth maul is actually a  member of the species known as  zabrak the signature facial markings of  darth maul set him apart from other  villains in the star wars movies  they fascinated fans and cosplayers  across the world and  inspired a great deal of speculation and  imitation  since maul was the first member of his  species introduced to audiences  and given the fact that the facial  markings look like they could be natural  many fans thought that the black stripes  were simply a part of his species  natural markings  like the ring of horns on his head or  his haunting eyes we all assumed that  this was a hallmark of whatever species  maul hailed from  but when more about his origin story was  revealed fans learned that  others of his species had similar  markings it turns out that the marks are  actually  tattoos given to young male zabrak  warriors  darth maul got his tattoos before his  first birthday by his mother talzin the  leader of the night sisters  there's nothing more symbolic of a  warrior aligned with the force  be it dark side or light side than a  lightsaber these weapons of pure force  energy have become wildly popular with  fans worldwide  and the lore surrounding them is complex  and fascinating part of the training of  a jedi apprentice is the construction of  their own lightsaber  while they build their weapons padawan  discovered that the true power of these  swords comes from something known  as a kyber crystal they're used to focus  force energy giving the lightsaber its  blade  the reason they're so precious to the  jedi and the sith is that these crystals  are naturally attuned to the force when  a young jedi finds the right  kyber crystal to craft their lightsaber  they meditate with the crystal  aligning themselves to it until it takes  on a unique  color but when a sith builds a  lightsaber it's a much more violent  affair  they steal the kyber crystal from a  defeated jedi and meditate with it  seeking to break its connection with the  light side and turn it to the dark side  of the force  this process is known as bleeding the  crystal and it gives the sith weapons  their distinctive red hue  so if you were wondering how darth  maul's lightsaber got its particular  color  now you know this is a big one if you've  seen the phantom menace and saw obi-wan  cutting darth maul down then you  probably assumed that the sith  apprentice was no more  at the battle of naboo qui-gon jinn and  obi-wan kenobi finally confront darth  maul  qui-gon falls to the sith's superior  lightsaber techniques as obi-wan watches  helplessly  then kenobi with the fury of the force  on his side  assaults the sith in an epic lightsaber  battle which ends in darth maul getting  neatly sliced in half  the gruesome image of maul's severed  body falling into a dark abyss stuck  with fans for years  and everybody believed they'd seen the  last of the sith apprentice  but as in so many movies and tv shows  falling into a misty  seemingly bottomless pit doesn't mean  much even if you've been chopped in two  years later it was revealed that darth  maul didn't die from his injuries that  day  he used his powerful ties to the force  as well as his sheer will  and an all-consuming hatred nourished by  his sith training to cling to life  my hatred get my spirit intact even  though my body was not  yet i was lost and became a rabid animal  maul escaped through a garbage chute and  along with trash was brought to a  landfill planet where he crudely  constructed a set of robotic spider-like  legs  losing his mind in the process it must  have been pretty reassuring for luke  skywalker the first time he heard his  departed mentor obi-wan kenobi's voice  after losing his aunt and uncle the only  home he'd ever known  and the man who introduced him to the  space magic the jedi called the force  it was probably a big relief to know  that there was a way for the dead to  communicate with the living  oddly being able to defy death is  supposed to be the hallmark of the sith  it's what initially attracted anakin  skywalker to the dark side after all  however only those who've devoted their  lives to the light side of the force can  return as force ghosts  and impart advice to those still  inhabiting the mortal realm  in other words darth maul can never come  back as a force ghost  sure by the end of his long and exciting  life he wasn't a fan of the sith  but he never embraced the light side of  the force  anakin skywalker also known as darth  vader was able to return as a force  ghost because  in the end he renounced evil and turned  to the light  darth maul he was bad to the bone until  the day he died  taken from his homeworld and everything  he knew at a young age darth maul was  trained by one of the most powerful sith  lords the galaxy has ever known  darth sidious molded maul to be a living  weapon and tool of the dark side  the intense training and brainwashing he  was subjected to was nearly impossible  to break away from  and at first it seemed that darth maul  would be loyal to the sith  until the day he died this wasn't the  case  remember when we told you that he  survived being cut in half on naboo  well eventually he was rescued by his  brother as he recovered he was given a  more traditional set of robotic legs to  replace the spider-like ones he had  constructed  once he had finally healed maul set his  mind to a singular objective  revenge against kenobi unfortunately by  the time he was ready for battle once  again  darth sidious had already taken on darth  vader as his new apprentice  for the sith there can be only two a  master  and an apprentice and since vader was in  maul  was out instead he used his force powers  and his prowess in battle to set himself  up as a crime lord  becoming the shadow power behind the  ruler of the planet mandalore  while lurking in exile building a  criminal empire maul never lost sight of  his one true burning motivation  revenge against the man who'd bested him  obi-wan kenobi  had taken almost everything from maul  after cutting him down on nobu  after briefly battling once again for a  long time it seemed like that encounter  would be the last time  the two would ever meet but years later  darth maul would have his final showdown  the two wove in and out of each other's  lives during the clone wars and beyond  but it would be on tatooine the location  of their first encounter  where maul would meet his doom at the  hands of kenobi  years after the fall of the galactic  republic maul traced kenobi to his  desert hideout  it was here that the jedi kept a  watchful eye on a growing luke skywalker  the two old foes crossed sabers once  again and the outcome  was the same kenobi stood triumphant  this time we're good check out one of  our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about star  wars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]  you

